{0 Error Handling Strategies}

Comprehensive guide to robust error handling in Telegram bots using Result types, retry logic with backoff, graceful degradation, and user-friendly error reporting.

{1 Overview}

Building resilient bots requires handling errors elegantly. The [ocaml_telegram_eio] library provides sophisticated error handling capabilities through:

- {b Type-safe error representation}: All errors are typed with {!Telegram.Error.t}
- {b Retryable vs non-retryable}: Automatic classification of transient vs permanent failures
- {b Retry strategies}: Exponential backoff, jitter, Telegram-aware rate limit handling
- {b Result types}: Explicit error propagation with [(result, Error.t) result]
- {b Error recovery}: Graceful degradation and fallback patterns
- {b User communication}: Clear, actionable error messages for end users

{2 When to Use This Guide}

Use these patterns when you need to:

- Handle network failures and timeouts gracefully
- Respect Telegram's rate limits and retry_after hints
- Distinguish between recoverable and permanent errors
- Provide helpful error messages to users
- Build fault-tolerant bots that recover from failures
- Implement retry logic with exponential backoff
- Handle API changes and migrations

{1 Error Types}

{2 Error Variants}

All Telegram API errors are represented by {!Telegram.Error.t}:

{[
type t =
  | Http_error of int * string
    (* HTTP-level errors: network failures, 5xx server errors *)
  | Api_error of { code : int; description : string; parameters : response_parameters option }
    (* Telegram API errors: 400 Bad Request, 403 Forbidden, 429 Too Many Requests *)
  | Decode_error of string
    (* JSON decoding failures: unexpected response format *)
  | Timeout
    (* Request timeout *)
  | Canceled
    (* Request canceled *)
  | Not_implemented of string
    (* Feature not implemented *)
]}

{2 Response Parameters}

Some errors include additional metadata:

{[
type response_parameters = {
  migrate_to_chat_id : Id.Chat.k Id.t option;
    (* For group migrations: new chat ID *)
  retry_after : int option;
    (* Rate limit hint: seconds to wait before retry *)
}
]}

{2 Retryable vs Non-Retryable Errors}

The library automatically classifies errors:

{[
(* Check if an error should be retried *)
let should_retry err =
  Error.is_retryable err

(* Examples of retryable errors:
   - Network timeouts
   - HTTP 5xx server errors
   - 429 Too Many Requests (rate limits)
   - Temporary service disruptions
*)

(* Examples of non-retryable errors:
   - 400 Bad Request (invalid parameters)
   - 401 Unauthorized (invalid token)
   - 403 Forbidden (bot blocked by user)
   - 404 Not Found (chat/message doesn't exist)
*)
]}

{2 Extracting Error Information}

{[
(* Get retry_after hint from rate limit errors *)
let handle_error err =
  match Error.retry_after err with
  | Some seconds ->
      Printf.printf "Rate limited. Retry after %d seconds\n" seconds
  | None ->
      Printf.eprintf "Error: %s\n" (Format.asprintf "%a" Error.pp err)

(* Get migration information *)
let handle_migration err =
  match Error.parameters err with
  | Some { migrate_to_chat_id = Some new_chat_id; _ } ->
      Printf.printf "Group migrated to: %Ld\n" (Id.Chat.to_int new_chat_id)
  | _ -> ()
]}

{1 Result Type Patterns}

{2 Basic Result Handling}

All API calls return [Result.t]:

{[
let send_message client chat_id text =
  match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () with
  | Ok message ->
      Printf.printf "Message sent: %d\n" message.message_id
  | Error err ->
      Printf.eprintf "Failed to send: %a\n" Error.pp err
]}

{2 Error Propagation with Bind}

Use monadic bind for composing operations:

{[
let open Result.Syntax in

let send_and_pin client chat_id text =
  (* Send message *)
  let* message = Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () in

  (* Pin the message *)
  let message_id = message.message_id in
  let* () = Gen_methods.pin_chat_message client ~chat_id ~message_id () in

  Ok message

(* Alternative: infix operator *)
let send_and_pin' client chat_id text =
  Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
  >>= fun message ->
  Gen_methods.pin_chat_message client ~chat_id ~message_id:message.message_id ()
  >>= fun () ->
  Ok message
]}

{2 Error Mapping and Transformation}

{[
(* Map errors to custom error types *)
let send_with_context client chat_id text =
  Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
  |> Result.map_error (fun err ->
      Printf.sprintf "Failed to send to chat %Ld: %a"
        (Id.Chat.to_int chat_id)
        Error.pp err
    )

(* Add context to errors *)
let broadcast_message client chat_ids text =
  List.map (fun chat_id ->
    Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
    |> Result.map_error (fun err -> (chat_id, err))
  ) chat_ids
]}

{2 Or_fail Pattern}

Convert Result to exception for cases where failure is unexpected:

{[
(* For initialization that must succeed *)
let init_bot token =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  let client = Client.create ~env ~token () in

  (* Get bot info - fail fast if token is invalid *)
  let me = Gen_methods.get_me client ()
           |> Error.or_fail in

  Printf.printf "Bot started: @%s\n"
    (Option.value me.username ~default:"unknown");

  client
]}

{1 Retry Strategies}

{2 Built-in Retry Strategies}

The {!Telegram.Retry} module provides composable retry strategies:

{[
(* Immediate retry - not recommended for production *)
let immediate = Retry.Strategy.immediate

(* Fixed delay between retries *)
let fixed = Retry.Strategy.fixed 2.0  (* 2 seconds *)

(* Exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s, ... up to max *)
let exponential =
  Retry.Strategy.exponential
    ~initial:1.0
    ~max:30.0
    ~multiplier:2.0
    ()

(* Exponential backoff with jitter (±10% randomness) *)
let with_jitter =
  Retry.Strategy.exponential_jitter
    ~initial:1.0
    ~max:30.0
    ~jitter:0.1
    ()

(* Telegram-aware: respects retry_after hints *)
let telegram_aware =
  Retry.Strategy.telegram_aware ()
]}

{2 Retry Configuration}

{[
(* Default configuration *)
let default_config = Retry.default
(* Uses exponential backoff, max 3 attempts *)

(* Custom configuration *)
let custom_config =
  Retry.make
    ~strategy:(Retry.Strategy.exponential_jitter ())
    ~max_attempts:5
    ~on_retry:(fun ~attempt ~error ~delay ->
      Printf.eprintf "Retry %d after %.1fs: %a\n"
        attempt delay Error.pp error
    )
    ()
]}

{2 Using Retry Logic}

{[
(* Retry with default configuration *)
let send_with_retry client chat_id text =
  Retry.with_default @@ fun () ->
    Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()

(* Retry with specific strategy *)
let send_with_backoff client chat_id text =
  let strategy = Retry.Strategy.exponential_jitter ~initial:0.5 ~max:10.0 () in
  Retry.with_strategy strategy @@ fun () ->
    Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()

(* Retry with custom config *)
let send_critical_message client chat_id text =
  let config =
    Retry.make
      ~strategy:(Retry.Strategy.telegram_aware ())
      ~max_attempts:10
      ~on_retry:(fun ~attempt ~error ~delay ->
        Printf.eprintf "[CRITICAL] Retry %d/%d after %.1fs\n"
          attempt 10 delay
      )
      ()
  in
  Retry.with_config config @@ fun () ->
    Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
]}

{2 Selective Retry}

Only retry on retryable errors:

{[
let send_with_selective_retry client chat_id text =
  let rec attempt n =
    match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () with
    | Ok msg -> Ok msg
    | Error err when Error.is_retryable err && n < 3 ->
        (* Wait and retry *)
        let delay = Float.of_int (1 lsl n) in  (* 2^n seconds *)
        Eio.Time.sleep (Eio.Stdenv.clock env) delay;
        attempt (n + 1)
    | Error err ->
        (* Non-retryable or max attempts reached *)
        Error err
  in
  attempt 0
]}

{1 Graceful Degradation}

{2 Fallback Values}

Provide defaults when operations fail:

{[
(* Get user info with fallback *)
let get_user_display_name client user_id =
  match Gen_methods.get_chat client ~chat_id:(Id.Chat.of_user user_id) () with
  | Ok chat -> Option.value chat.first_name ~default:"User"
  | Error _ -> "User"  (* Fallback on error *)

(* Try multiple methods *)
let send_notification client chat_id text =
  (* Try sending with preview *)
  match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () with
  | Ok msg -> Ok msg
  | Error _ ->
      (* Fallback: send without preview *)
      Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text
        ~disable_web_page_preview:true ()
]}

{2 Partial Success Handling}

{[
(* Broadcast to multiple chats, collecting failures *)
let broadcast client chat_ids text =
  let results = List.map (fun chat_id ->
    (chat_id, Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ())
  ) chat_ids in

  let successes = List.filter_map (fun (id, res) ->
    match res with Ok msg -> Some (id, msg) | Error _ -> None
  ) results in

  let failures = List.filter_map (fun (id, res) ->
    match res with Error err -> Some (id, err) | Ok _ -> None
  ) results in

  Printf.printf "Broadcast: %d/%d succeeded\n"
    (List.length successes) (List.length chat_ids);

  (successes, failures)
]}

{2 Circuit Breaker Pattern}

{[
type circuit_state = Closed | Open | HalfOpen

type circuit_breaker = {
  mutable state : circuit_state;
  mutable failure_count : int;
  mutable last_failure_time : float;
  failure_threshold : int;
  timeout : float;
}

let create_circuit_breaker ~failure_threshold ~timeout =
  { state = Closed; failure_count = 0;
    last_failure_time = 0.0; failure_threshold; timeout }

let call_with_circuit_breaker breaker f =
  let now = Unix.gettimeofday () in

  match breaker.state with
  | Open when now -. breaker.last_failure_time > breaker.timeout ->
      (* Try transitioning to half-open *)
      breaker.state <- HalfOpen;
      call_with_circuit_breaker breaker f

  | Open ->
      (* Circuit is open, fail fast *)
      Error (Error.Api_error {
        code = 503;
        description = "Service temporarily unavailable (circuit breaker open)";
        parameters = None
      })

  | Closed | HalfOpen ->
      match f () with
      | Ok result ->
          (* Success: reset circuit *)
          breaker.state <- Closed;
          breaker.failure_count <- 0;
          Ok result

      | Error err when Error.is_retryable err ->
          (* Failure: increment counter *)
          breaker.failure_count <- breaker.failure_count + 1;
          breaker.last_failure_time <- now;

          if breaker.failure_count >= breaker.failure_threshold then
            breaker.state <- Open;

          Error err

      | Error err ->
          (* Non-retryable: don't count against circuit *)
          Error err

(* Usage *)
let breaker = create_circuit_breaker ~failure_threshold:5 ~timeout:60.0

let send_with_circuit_breaker client chat_id text =
  call_with_circuit_breaker breaker @@ fun () ->
    Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
]}

{1 Error Reporting to Users}

{2 User-Friendly Error Messages}

{[
(* Convert errors to user-readable messages *)
let error_to_user_message err =
  match err with
  | Error.Api_error { code = 403; description; _ } ->
      if String.contains description "blocked" then
        "I cannot send you messages. Please unblock me and try again."
      else
        "I don't have permission to perform this action."

  | Error.Api_error { code = 400; description; _ } ->
      if String.contains description "message is not modified" then
        "This message is already up to date."
      else if String.contains description "text is empty" then
        "Please provide some text."
      else
        "Invalid request. Please check your input."

  | Error.Api_error { code = 429; parameters = Some { retry_after = Some sec; _ }; _ } ->
      Printf.sprintf "Too many requests. Please try again in %d seconds." sec

  | Error.Timeout ->
      "Request timed out. Please try again."

  | Error.Http_error (code, _) when code >= 500 ->
      "Telegram servers are temporarily unavailable. Please try again later."

  | _ ->
      "Sorry, an error occurred while processing your request."

(* Send error notification to user *)
let notify_user_of_error client chat_id err =
  let message = error_to_user_message err in
  let _ = Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text:message () in
  ()
]}

{2 Error Handling in Bot DSL}

{[
(* Route-level error handler *)
let my_route =
  Bot.on Event.message (fun msg ctx ->
    (* Handler code that might fail *)
    match process_message msg with
    | Ok () -> ()
    | Error err ->
        let user_msg = error_to_user_message err in
        let _ = Ctx.reply ctx user_msg in
        ()
  )
  |> Bot.with_error_handler (fun ctx exn ->
      let err_msg = "Sorry, something went wrong: " ^ Printexc.to_string exn in
      let _ = Ctx.reply ctx err_msg in
      ()
    )

(* Global error handler *)
let routes =
  Bot.router
    ~on_error:(fun ctx exn ->
      (* Log error *)
      Printf.eprintf "Error in handler: %s\n" (Printexc.to_string exn);

      (* Notify user *)
      let _ = Ctx.reply ctx "An error occurred. Please try again." in
      ()
    )
    [ route1; route2; route3 ]
]}

{2 Built-in Error Handlers}

{[
(* Log errors to stderr *)
let with_logging =
  Bot.with_error_handler Bot.ErrorHandler.log route

(* Log and send user notification *)
let with_user_feedback =
  Bot.with_error_handler
    (Bot.ErrorHandler.log_and_reply ~message:"Oops! Something went wrong." ())
    route

(* Silent error handling (not recommended) *)
let silent =
  Bot.with_error_handler Bot.ErrorHandler.silent route

(* Combine multiple error handlers *)
let combined =
  Bot.with_error_handler
    (Bot.ErrorHandler.combine [
      Bot.ErrorHandler.log;
      Bot.ErrorHandler.log_and_reply ();
    ])
    route
]}

{1 Advanced Error Patterns}

{2 Error Categorization}

{[
type error_category =
  | Transient     (* Retry immediately or with backoff *)
  | RateLimited   (* Respect retry_after hint *)
  | UserError     (* Notify user, don't retry *)
  | BotError      (* Log for developer, notify user *)
  | Fatal         (* Stop bot, alert admin *)

let categorize_error err =
  match err with
  | Error.Timeout | Error.Http_error (code, _) when code >= 500 ->
      Transient

  | Error.Api_error { code = 429; _ } ->
      RateLimited

  | Error.Api_error { code = 400; _ } | Error.Api_error { code = 403; _ } ->
      UserError

  | Error.Decode_error _ | Error.Not_implemented _ ->
      BotError

  | Error.Api_error { code = 401; _ } ->
      Fatal

  | _ ->
      BotError

(* Handle based on category *)
let handle_categorized_error client chat_id err =
  match categorize_error err with
  | Transient ->
      (* Retry with backoff *)
      Printf.eprintf "Transient error, will retry: %a\n" Error.pp err

  | RateLimited ->
      (* Wait for retry_after *)
      begin match Error.retry_after err with
      | Some seconds ->
          Printf.eprintf "Rate limited, waiting %d seconds\n" seconds;
          Eio.Time.sleep (Eio.Stdenv.clock env) (Float.of_int seconds)
      | None ->
          Eio.Time.sleep (Eio.Stdenv.clock env) 1.0
      end

  | UserError ->
      (* Notify user *)
      let msg = error_to_user_message err in
      let _ = Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text:msg () in
      ()

  | BotError ->
      (* Log and notify user *)
      Printf.eprintf "Bot error: %a\n" Error.pp err;
      let _ = Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id
        ~text:"An internal error occurred." () in
      ()

  | Fatal ->
      (* Alert admin and stop *)
      Printf.eprintf "FATAL ERROR: %a\n" Error.pp err;
      exit 1
]}

{2 Error Recovery Pipeline}

{[
(* Attempt operations with fallback chain *)
let send_with_recovery client chat_id text =
  (* Try 1: Send normally *)
  match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text () with
  | Ok msg -> Ok msg
  | Error err1 ->
      Printf.eprintf "Attempt 1 failed: %a\n" Error.pp err1;

      (* Try 2: Send without preview *)
      match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text
              ~disable_web_page_preview:true () with
      | Ok msg -> Ok msg
      | Error err2 ->
          Printf.eprintf "Attempt 2 failed: %a\n" Error.pp err2;

          (* Try 3: Send truncated text *)
          let short_text = String.sub text 0 (min 200 (String.length text)) in
          match Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text:short_text () with
          | Ok msg -> Ok msg
          | Error err3 ->
              (* All attempts failed *)
              Printf.eprintf "All recovery attempts failed\n";
              Error err3
]}

{2 Error Metrics and Monitoring}

{[
type error_metrics = {
  mutable total_errors : int;
  mutable retryable_errors : int;
  mutable non_retryable_errors : int;
  mutable rate_limit_errors : int;
  errors_by_code : (int, int) Hashtbl.t;
}

let create_metrics () = {
  total_errors = 0;
  retryable_errors = 0;
  non_retryable_errors = 0;
  rate_limit_errors = 0;
  errors_by_code = Hashtbl.create 16;
}

let record_error metrics err =
  metrics.total_errors <- metrics.total_errors + 1;

  if Error.is_retryable err then
    metrics.retryable_errors <- metrics.retryable_errors + 1
  else
    metrics.non_retryable_errors <- metrics.non_retryable_errors + 1;

  begin match err with
  | Error.Api_error { code = 429; _ } ->
      metrics.rate_limit_errors <- metrics.rate_limit_errors + 1
  | Error.Api_error { code; _ } ->
      let count = Hashtbl.find_opt metrics.errors_by_code code |> Option.value ~default:0 in
      Hashtbl.replace metrics.errors_by_code code (count + 1)
  | _ -> ()
  end

let print_metrics metrics =
  Printf.printf "Error Metrics:\n";
  Printf.printf "  Total: %d\n" metrics.total_errors;
  Printf.printf "  Retryable: %d (%.1f%%)\n"
    metrics.retryable_errors
    (100.0 *. Float.of_int metrics.retryable_errors /. Float.of_int metrics.total_errors);
  Printf.printf "  Non-retryable: %d (%.1f%%)\n"
    metrics.non_retryable_errors
    (100.0 *. Float.of_int metrics.non_retryable_errors /. Float.of_int metrics.total_errors);
  Printf.printf "  Rate limits: %d\n" metrics.rate_limit_errors;
  Printf.printf "  By code:\n";
  Hashtbl.iter (fun code count ->
    Printf.printf "    %d: %d\n" code count
  ) metrics.errors_by_code
]}

{1 Production Examples}

{2 Resilient Broadcast System}

{[
(* Broadcast with retry, rate limiting, and progress tracking *)
let broadcast_message client chat_ids text =
  let total = List.length chat_ids in
  let metrics = create_metrics () in
  let successful = ref 0 in
  let failed = ref [] in

  (* Rate limit: max 30 messages per second *)
  let semaphore = Eio.Semaphore.make 30 in
  let clock = Eio.Stdenv.clock env in

  List.iteri (fun i chat_id ->
    (* Acquire rate limit token *)
    Eio.Semaphore.acquire semaphore;

    (* Send with retry *)
    let result = Retry.with_default @@ fun () ->
      Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text ()
    in

    (* Process result *)
    begin match result with
    | Ok _ ->
        successful := !successful + 1;
        Printf.printf "\rProgress: %d/%d (%.1f%%) ✓"
          (i + 1) total (100.0 *. Float.of_int (i + 1) /. Float.of_int total);
        flush stdout

    | Error err ->
        record_error metrics err;
        failed := (chat_id, err) :: !failed;
        Printf.printf "\rProgress: %d/%d (%.1f%%) ✗"
          (i + 1) total (100.0 *. Float.of_int (i + 1) /. Float.of_int total);
        flush stdout
    end;

    (* Release token after 1 second *)
    Eio.Fiber.fork ~sw (fun () ->
      Eio.Time.sleep clock 1.0;
      Eio.Semaphore.release semaphore
    )
  ) chat_ids;

  Printf.printf "\n\nBroadcast complete:\n";
  Printf.printf "  Successful: %d/%d\n" !successful total;
  Printf.printf "  Failed: %d/%d\n" (List.length !failed) total;
  print_metrics metrics;

  (!successful, !failed)
]}

{2 Error-Tolerant Poll Handler}

{[
let handle_update_with_recovery client update =
  let handle () =
    match update.Update.message with
    | Some msg ->
        let chat_id = Id.Chat.of_int msg.Message.chat.Chat.id in
        let text = Option.value msg.Message.text ~default:"" in

        if text <> "" then
          (* Try to echo with retry *)
          let response = "You said: " ^ text in
          Retry.with_config
            (Retry.make ~strategy:(Retry.Strategy.telegram_aware ()) ~max_attempts:3 ())
            (fun () -> Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text:response ())
        else
          Ok ()

    | None -> Ok ()
  in

  match handle () with
  | Ok _ -> ()
  | Error err ->
      (* Log error but continue processing updates *)
      Printf.eprintf "Error handling update: %a\n" Error.pp err;

      (* Try to notify user if possible *)
      begin match update.Update.message with
      | Some msg ->
          let chat_id = Id.Chat.of_int msg.Message.chat.Chat.id in
          let user_msg = error_to_user_message err in
          let _ = Gen_methods.send_message client ~chat_id ~text:user_msg () in
          ()
      | None -> ()
      end
]}

{2 Production Bot with Full Error Handling}

{[
let run_production_bot token =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->

  (* Create client *)
  let client = Client.create ~env ~token () in

  (* Verify token on startup *)
  let me =
    Retry.with_default (fun () -> Gen_methods.get_me client ())
    |> Error.or_fail
  in
  Printf.printf "Bot started: @%s\n"
    (Option.value me.username ~default:"unknown");

  (* Error metrics *)
  let metrics = create_metrics () in

  (* Define error handler *)
  let handle_error ctx exn =
    Printf.eprintf "Handler error: %s\n" (Printexc.to_string exn);

    (* Send user notification *)
    let _ = Ctx.reply ctx "An error occurred. Please try again later." in
    ()
  in

  (* Define routes with error handling *)
  let routes =
    Bot.router ~on_error:handle_error [
      Bot.on (Event.command "start") (fun cmd ctx ->
        match Ctx.reply ctx "Welcome! I'm a resilient bot with robust error handling." with
        | Ok _ -> ()
        | Error err ->
            record_error metrics err;
            handle_error ctx (Failure (Format.asprintf "%a" Error.pp err))
      );

      Bot.on Event.message (fun msg ctx ->
        let text = Option.value msg.text ~default:"" in

        (* Process with retry *)
        let result = Retry.with_default @@ fun () ->
          (* Echo back *)
          Ctx.reply ctx ("Echo: " ^ text)
        in

        match result with
        | Ok _ -> ()
        | Error err ->
            record_error metrics err;

            (* Notify user based on error category *)
            match categorize_error err with
            | UserError | BotError ->
                let user_msg = error_to_user_message err in
                let _ = Ctx.reply ctx user_msg in
                ()
            | Fatal ->
                Printf.eprintf "FATAL: %a\n" Error.pp err;
                exit 1
            | _ -> ()
      );
    ]
  in

  (* Run with polling *)
  Printf.printf "Starting polling...\n";
  Bot.run_polling ~env ~client routes;

  (* Print metrics on shutdown *)
  print_metrics metrics
]}

{1 Best Practices}

{2 Error Handling Design}

- {b Use Result types}: Never throw exceptions for expected errors
- {b Classify errors}: Distinguish retryable from permanent failures
- {b Fail fast on fatal errors}: Invalid tokens, missing permissions
- {b Retry transient errors}: Network issues, server errors, rate limits
- {b Respect retry_after}: Use [Retry.Strategy.telegram_aware] for production
- {b Provide context}: Include relevant information when propagating errors
- {b Log appropriately}: Debug details for developers, friendly messages for users

{2 Retry Strategy Selection}

- {b Development}: Use [Retry.Strategy.fixed] for predictable behavior
- {b Production}: Use [Retry.Strategy.telegram_aware] to respect rate limits
- {b High-volume bots}: Use [Retry.Strategy.exponential_jitter] to avoid thundering herd
- {b Critical operations}: Increase max_attempts for important messages
- {b Batch operations}: Implement circuit breaker to avoid cascading failures

{2 User Communication}

- {b Be specific}: "Too many requests" vs "An error occurred"
- {b Be actionable}: Tell users what they can do
- {b Be honest}: Don't hide errors, but don't show stack traces
- {b Provide retry hints}: "Please try again in 30 seconds"
- {b Log internally}: Keep detailed logs for debugging

{2 Graceful Degradation}

- {b Provide fallbacks}: Degraded functionality is better than no functionality
- {b Handle partial failures}: Don't fail entire batch on single error
- {b Cache when possible}: Serve stale data rather than fail
- {b Circuit breaker}: Stop hammering failing services
- {b Monitor and alert}: Track error rates and patterns

{2 Testing Error Handling}

- {b Test all error paths}: Don't just test happy path
- {b Simulate failures}: Network errors, timeouts, rate limits
- {b Test recovery}: Verify retry logic works correctly
- {b Test user feedback}: Ensure error messages are helpful
- {b Monitor in production}: Track error metrics and patterns

